        ],
        "params": {
          "text": "SMALL-ANGLE DOUBLE PENDULUM / SLOW MODE / SYMPLECTIC\nm1=m2=l1=l2=1, g=9.81; theta1''=-2g*theta1+g*theta2; theta2''=2g*theta1-2g*theta2.\nInitial angles: 0.1, 0.1414213562373095 rad; velocities zero. Default h=0.001 s. Run for 20 s at 1, 10 and 100 kHz.\nVelocity-first semi-implicit Euler; each acceleration uses both old angles.\nNormal frequencies: sqrt(g*(2-sqrt(2))), sqrt(g*(2+sqrt(2))). After step k, plotted state is z[k-1]; runtime timestamp is k*h. See README.md.",
          "width": 2100.0,
          "height": 180.0,
          "font_size": 10
        }
      }
